# Runs on every push. CI is manual-only, so this hook is the always-on enforcement: the backend's
# architecture specs hold the repo's rules (layer boundaries, schema conventions, the error envelope).
# The foundation packages are built first because the backend reads them through their dist; turbo
# skips the build when nothing changed. The web app's own guards run after them: one component set
# (apps/web/src/shared/components/__tests__/single-component-set.test.ts), the theme-token contrast
# (apps/web/src/shared/components/page-chrome/__tests__/theme-tokens.test.ts) and the UI grammar
# (apps/web/src/features/__tests__/ui-grammar-guard.test.ts).
pnpm verify:arch

# The ops checks (`pnpm check:ops`: the Grafana-as-code catalog, the ops shell tests, Terraform) run when the pushed
# commits touch the files they check: infra/, docs/runbooks/, .github/ or tools/. `pnpm verify` runs them every time.
if bash tools/verify/push-touches-ops.sh; then
  pnpm check:ops
fi

# The repository guards (tools/guards, Node only, seconds): skills, agents, docs and source comments cite only files,
# symbols, skills and guards that exist, and every workflow keeps CI manual (.claude/workflow.json). Then their tests.
pnpm guards
pnpm test:guards
